# The voyage itself: wonder, home, ship life, the dark, the approach.
# Arc, threads and plants: content/STORY_BIBLE.md (spoilers). Voice: content/STYLE.md.
# Personal threads: each `who ow_*` opener casts a different astronaut (`!is`), and
# that astronaut carries the thread to its payoff and epilogue line.

# --- Leaving -------------------------------------------------------------------
card p_live_call
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 1 1
roles A
text {A} calls home while the delay is still under a second. Someone tells a bad joke and {A} laughs on the beat, in real time, with everyone at the table. Afterwards {A} writes down who was there and what they ate, and folds the list into a flight-suit pocket.
do who ow_list A
do morale A 5

card p_music
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 2 2
roles A
when !is A ow_list
text {A} plays the same four bars on a travel guitar at the end of every watch, into the fleet channel, never the rest of the song. By the last top-off tanker seven ships are guessing at the fifth bar, seven different ways.
do who ow_song A
do trait A warm 1

card l_reboot
type beat
cat life
clue core
due
once
days 3 5
roles A
text The galley screen on {A}'s ship takes a 2.3-gigabyte update overnight and restarts at breakfast: the logo, a progress bar, the three-note chime, all over before {A} has counted to eleven. Then it logs out again. By departure the whole fleet is humming the chime.
do morale A 1
do who abort_who A

card l_dock_hello
type beat
cat life
clue core
due
once
days 12 12
roles A
text Crossing window. The next ship's hatch takes a code that goes stale in a fifth of a second. The procedure still says to read them up via the ground. {A} does, once: CODE STALE. Ship to ship it opens first time, and {A} files a correction to page two.
do trait A curious 1

card p_garden_plant
type beat
cat life
due
once
days 4 4
roles A
when !is A ow_list
when !is A ow_song
text {A} plants the garden: six seed pods in a tray the size of a laptop, under a lamp the colour of a plum. {A} labels each pod in tiny capitals and says good night to them on an open channel. Several people say good night back.
do who ow_garden A
do var garden 1

card l_manifest
type beat
cat life
clue core
due
once
days 5 7
roles A
text {A} reads the manifest like a shopping list: water on Cargo 3, rover on Cargo 4. Write-offs: a grey relay, "thruster stuck open"; the last window's hopper, "tipped, beacon intermittent"; Cargo 2, drill spares, "lost on landing, scar in a low-res pass"; socks, "reason unknown".
do trait A curious 1

card l_departure
type beat
cat wonder
due
once
days 6 6
roles A
text The last tanker undocks at dawn. Eight ships light their engines, and {A} feels weight come back. The timeline calls the burn COMMIT: after it, every way home runs past Mars. From here the log keeps one page for every five days; by the next page {A} can hide Earth behind a thumb.
do morale A 3

card l_transfer
type beat
cat life
due
once
days 2 2
roles A
text Ships fly a few kilometres apart, one seat a ship, so no single failure takes two people; a visit bends the rule and is logged. Votes advise; the flight director decides. Every few weeks ships close up for a tethered crossing. {A} goes first, and logs it: "Recommended. Hold on."
do trait A brave 2

card l_handshake
type beat
cat life
due
once
days 13 36
roles A
when is A abort_who
when home A
text The galley screen on {A}'s ship has started to sulk: after every restart it sits on its logo longer than it used to, then boots with a sad cloud icon and the word OFFLINE. {A} files a ticket titled "manners".
do morale A 1

# --- Thread: the list ------------------------------------------------------------
card p_list_letter
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 18 19
roles A
when is A ow_list
text The delay has turned calls into letters. {A} records one for home, deletes it, tries again with pauses, which is worse, then goes at speed: "Hi, it's me, ship's fine, I'm fine, the fans hum in a key now, here's the list," and that one goes.
do morale A 2
do trait A warm 2

card p_packer_note
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 16 17
roles A
when flag stash_kept
when is A stash_who
when !flag stash_exposed
text A voice note from the Starbase loading crew reaches {A}, a forklift beeping. The one who packed the bags: "Eat the good rations first. The bad ones keep. And say hello to the hardware for us. It sulks if no one does." {A} checks the locker. True.
do morale A 2

card p_packer_note_g
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 16 17
roles A
when !is A ow_list
when !flag stash_kept
text A voice note from the Starbase loading crew reaches {A}, a forklift beeping. The one who packed the bags: "Eat the good rations first. The bad ones keep. And say hello to the hardware for us. It sulks if no one does." {A} checks the galley log: the good rations went first, fleet-wide. True.
do morale A 2

card g_news
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 27 28
roles A
when is A ow_list
text A message from home for {A}: a retirement party, already over, for the neighbour who always brought the folding chairs, a name from the first call's list. They're moving to the sea. Someone saved {A} a chair. {A} watches the recording to the end and asks for the next watch.
do morale A -8
do trait A warm 3

card c_list
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 35 36
roles A
when is A ow_list
text {A} copies the list from the first call into the entry notes, name by name, and reaches the end feeling it's short. It is: the person who held the phone up that night never made it onto the list, because they were holding the phone. {A} adds them at the top.
do morale A 3

card a_list
type beat
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when is A ow_list
text {A} writes to every name on the list from the first call, one to the folding chairs at a new address by the sea, and a last one to a loading bay at Starbase. Each will land eight minutes after it's sent. {A} sends them without a single pause: no ums, no gaps, no saving the good bit for last.
do morale A 3

# --- Thread: the song ------------------------------------------------------------
card p_song_ask
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 21 22
roles A B
when is A ow_song
text On the night {B} finally asks about the four bars, {A} plays them again, all four, and stops. "Planet first." {B} says that's a deal, and starts humming a made-up fifth bar on purpose.
do bond A B 5
do bond B A 3

card c_song
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 36 37
roles A
when is A ow_song
text Alone, with the channel off, {A} tries a fifth bar after the four and gets it wrong. Then wrong again, differently. {A} puts the guitar back in its bag. "Not yet," {A} tells the guitar. "Entry morning."
do trait A warm 1

card a_song
type beat
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when is A ow_song
text On the last morning before the air, with a planet under the fleet again, {A} plays past the four bars, all the way through, and this time on the channel. Seven ships hear the fifth bar at last: it falls where they all had it rising, and lands on the beat the old channel keeps. "That's the one," {A} says.
do morale A 5

# --- Thread: the garden ------------------------------------------------------------
card p_garden_tend
type beat
cat life
once
days 8 20
weight 10
roles A
when is A ow_garden
text {A} waters the garden tray with a syringe, two millilitres per pod, and checks each one under the lamp. Nothing yet. {A} writes it down: "Nothing yet. Good, even nothing." Then tells the pods so.
do var garden 1

card p_garden_fail
type beat
cat grim
due
once
days 19 20
roles A
when is A ow_garden
text Four of the six pods have gone soft and grey: drowned. The schedule came from a book written for windowsills, where water drains away. Up here it just sits. {A} lifts them out with tweezers. "Wrong book," {A} tells the tray. "Let's go again." Half a dose, now, for the other two.
do morale A -3
do trait A warm 2

card p_garden_tend2
type beat
cat life
once
days 21 29
weight 8
roles A
when is A ow_garden
when !flag water_rationed
when !fired water_fail
text {A} waters the last two pods morning and night, and has started reading the seed packet's small print for encouragement. There isn't any, so {A} reads them the planting depth instead, with feeling.
do var garden 1

card p_garden_sprout
type beat
cat wonder
due
once
days 30 37
roles A
when is A ow_garden
when var garden >= 3
text {A} opens the fleet channel and turns the camera on the tray. In the last pod, a pale hook of a shoot has split the seed coat and turned, against no gravity at all, toward the lamp. Seven ships screenshot it at once.
do morale A 6

card c_garden
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 37 38
roles A
when is A ow_garden
when fired p_garden_sprout
text The entry checklist says loose items go in the locker. {A} reads it, puts the seedling's tray in the locker, and takes it straight back out. One cargo strap later it rides beside the seat. "It comes with me," {A} tells the flight surgeon, who has stopped arguing.
do morale A 3

card p_garden_none
type beat
cat grim
due
once
days 37 37
roles A
when is A ow_garden
when !fired p_garden_sprout
text The last pod never came up. Under the lamp the seed coat is whole, dry and patient, as if it had decided to wait for the ground. {A} keeps watering the tray, two millilitres, on schedule, and packs the seed in a coat pocket. Seeds keep.
do trait A warm 2

# --- The middle dark ------------------------------------------------------------
card w_venus_shadow
type event
cat wonder
days 7 10
weight 6
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text Lights off, the Sun behind the hull, {A}'s hand throws a shadow on the bulkhead, so faint {A} has to move the hand to see it. The light source is Venus. {A} makes a rabbit, then an open hand, letting the planet cast it.
do trait A curious 3

card w_phosphene
type beat
once
cat grim
days 19 23
weight 6
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} shuts both eyes in the bunk and sees a white spark, then another. Cosmic rays, passing straight through the eye, fast enough to make light; cameras see them too, as single bright pixels. {A} counts them like sheep, and loses count in the twenties.
do trait A curious 2
do morale A -1

card l_crystals
type event
cat grim
once
weight 40
days 20 28
roles A
when cond A ok
when home A
text The protein crystals in {A}'s locker, two years of a lab's work, cook overnight when the freezer fan seizes. {A} calls the lab, who ask for photos anyway. There is no second batch, and no second flight for it. {A} lights the photos properly, like evidence.
do morale A -3

card p_birthday
type beat
cat life
days 8 39
weight 7
once
roles A B
when same A B
when !fired beat_haircut
when away A
when home B
text A birthday by somebody's ground calendar; the fleet has stopped checking whose. {A}, aboard {B}'s ship, produces a candle that can't be lit, a ration-bar cake with a slice of dried mango, and a card signed by the whole fleet. {B} keeps the candle.
do bond A B 6
do morale B 5

card p_movie
type beat
cat life
days 7 39
weight 7
once
roles A B
when same A B
text Movie night with {B} over the link, a tablet on each ceiling, synced on a countdown: {A} picked a film set on a submarine. Halfway through, {A}'s hull ticks as the ship turns out of the sun. {A} pauses both screens, and they listen until it stops. Then {A} puts on something with a sky in it.
do bond A B 4

card p_dream
type beat
once
cat human
days 10 39
weight 5
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} wakes from a dream of rain on a car roof and lies still, trying to keep the sound. The fans hum. By breakfast the rain has gone. {A} writes "rain, car roof" in the log margin, in case it comes back.
do morale A -2
do trait A warm 2

card l_long_table
type event
cat life
due
once
days 7 7
roles A
when cond A ok
text Once a week the fleet eats together on video: eight tablets on eight galley tables, one meal at one time. {A} has the toast. It is eleven words long, and the table lets it stand.
do morale A 3

card l_long_table2
type event
cat life
days 26 38
weight 6
once
roles A B
when cond A ok
when is A ow_list
when cond B ok
text Long table night. {B} has the toast and gives it to the empty second chair at each of the eight tables. It lands on every screen at once, the one conversation out here with no delay. {A} laughs on the beat.
do morale A 3

card g_third_quarter
type event
cat grim
days 27 34
weight 9
once
roles A B
when cond A ok
when cond B ok
when !is B ow_list
text The flight surgeon calls it the third-quarter effect. On the video link {A} and {B} find themselves on the same checklist page at the same minute, both stuck on step four. {A} reads the steps aloud and {B} answers each one. They file a ticket: the page is too long.
do bond A B 6
do morale B 3

card g_margin
type beat
cat grim
days 18 26
weight 6
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text The flight surgeon's weekly sheet grows a column: days each ship lasts alone if the next crossing fails. {A}'s number is the shortest. {A} folds the sheet, numbers in, and files it behind the spare socks.
do trait A brave 1

card g_count
type beat
cat grim
days 21 39
weight 5
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} counts the medical kit against the manifest: sutures, splints, pain tablets in neat blister rows, and at the bottom, folded flat and vacuum-sealed, the line item the manifest calls "contingency, crew, 1". There is one on every ship. {A} signs for the count and closes the lid.
do trait A brave 2

card g_packer
type event
cat human
due
once
days 28 28
roles A
when is A ow_theory
text A batch of photos from the Starbase loading crew reaches {A}: the bay, the cranes, a forklift with a name, on charge at the service port at the foot of a cargo ship's leg. The same handwriting signs off: "Eight of you. Write when you land, every one." {A} clips the forklift inside the logbook.
do morale A 2

card sharpie2
type beat
cat human
days 26 39
weight 12
once
roles A
when fired dil_stash
when cond A ok
text Under the last tray in the spares locker, {A} finds a roll of tape that isn't on any list, and under it a laminated card in a bag: an old handshake procedure, headed in the same Sharpie hand: "Old manners, for old hardware." Down the margin, half under the tape: "...INSIDE ONE TICK."
do res spares 1
do morale A 5

# --- The approach --------------------------------------------------------------
card w_aurora
type event
cat wonder
days 33 39
weight 9
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text In one of the orbiters' night frames {A} finds a faint green smear over dark ground: Martian aurora, patchy, pinned to old magnetized rock no hand has ever touched. {A} sends it to the geology team, subject line: "look".
do trait A curious 3

card w_phobos
type event
cat wonder
days 37 39
weight 14
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text Phobos is a speck beside Mars on the long-lens camera now, slipping behind the disc and out the other side in under an hour. {A} watches it cross a whole world in the time of a meal, and wants weight, suddenly, more than sleep.
do trait A curious 2
do morale A 3

card w_mars_disc
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when flag c2_answered
when !is A ow_hail
when !is A ow_dose
when !is A ow_theory
text {A} holds a thumb up to the window, the old Earth-watch habit. Mars still fits behind it, for a few more nights: half rust, half dark, the dawn line ruled almost straight down the middle. Just past that line, too small to see, a light is holding steady.
do morale A 5

card w_mars_disc_q
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when !flag c2_answered
when !is A ow_hail
when !is A ow_dose
when !is A ow_theory
text {A} holds a thumb up to the window, the old Earth-watch habit. Mars still fits behind it, for a few more nights: half rust, half dark, the dawn line ruled almost straight down the middle. Just past that line, too small to see, a light is keeping time.
do morale A 5

card a_last_night
type beat
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A B
when is A ow_dose
when !flag arrive_wait
text The last nights before entry. {A} checks the water tanks that shielded the bunk all these weeks, by hand, the way you'd pat a horse. On the fleet channel {B} is doing the same on another ship. "Same time tomorrow?" {B} asks. "On the ground," {A} says. "One way or the other." {B} sets an alarm for it.
do bond A B 6

card a_last_night_o
type beat
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A B
when is A ow_dose
when flag arrive_wait
text The last nights before aerocapture. {A} checks the water tanks that shielded the bunk all these weeks, by hand, the way you'd pat a horse. On the fleet channel {B} is doing the same on another ship. "Same time tomorrow?" {B} asks. "In orbit," {A} says. "Then the ground. Then we'll see."
do bond A B 6

# --- Arrival day: what the fleet chose, and what it cost ------------------------------
card a_recall_photo
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 38 38
roles A
when flag photo_taken
text {A} stows the tablet with the fleet portrait on it: seven ships and the edge of an eighth, Earth behind them, and the propellant it took to fly them that close, which the last tanker quietly put back. Worth it, {A} decides; the tanker crew got a print.

card a_recall_wrist
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 37 37
roles A
when fired crisis_eva
when is A eva_who
text {A} runs the first entry seat checks with the wrist that wouldn't bend, mostly bending now, and reports it to the flight surgeon as "bending", with the angle in degrees. The surgeon clears the seat.

card a_recall_valve
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 39 39
roles A
when flag valve_out
when is A valve_who
when !is A abort_who
text Before the descent brief {A} flies the valve workaround once more in the simulator. The model rolls the wrong way on the flip before the landing burn, one jet short, and comes back, the way it did that night. {A} initials the log line and closes the panel.

card a_recall_shared
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 38 38
roles A B
when flag stash_exposed
when is A stash_who
when !is B stash_b
text Before the crossings closed, {A} sent {B} the last spare ration pack, the bag signed in borrowed handwriting: "You'll thank me." Tonight {B} opens it. Under the food, the little ship again, on red ground now, fingers still crossed. {B} eats every crumb and clips the drawing inside the logbook.
do bond B A 3

card a_recall_marker
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 41 41
roles A
when is A ow_theory
text {A} uncaps the blue marker one last time and adds a second lighthouse to the drawing: small, standing on the ground, and beside it a figure holding a marker. Then {A} folds it into a chest pocket with the marker.
do morale A 2

card a_suit_plan
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when flag signal_ignored
when is A ow_hail
when cond A ok
text {A} packs a handheld radio into a suit thigh pocket, retuned to the old channel, the old key loaded and checked by the ground, and the laminated card from under the spares tray, HELLO then HOLD. "First one out goes to say hello," {A} tells the ground. The ground says yes, if a spare battery rides along.
do morale A 3

# --- Day 42: the entry itself, last on the page; one scene per arrival branch, told by whoever was drilled on taking the landing by hand.
card e_entry_hold
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when flag arrive_hold
when flag c2_answered
when is A abort_who
text Entry interface. Three minutes of blackout, eight ships silent in turn. Below twenty kilometres the cameras see only brown. {A}'s ship slews in a gust the model never had. The radar has had the ground since eight kilometres; Cargo 2's ping, on two antennas, holds the bearing till the rim cuts it. At three hundred metres a slope comes up out of the brown; {A} calls the manual takeover before the plume takes the view.
do morale A 3

card e_entry_hold_q
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when flag arrive_hold
when !flag c2_answered
when is A abort_who
text Entry interface. Three minutes of blackout, eight ships silent in turn. Below twenty kilometres the cameras see only brown. {A}'s ship slews in a gust the model never had. The radar has had the ground since eight kilometres. At three hundred metres a slope comes up out of the brown; {A} calls the manual takeover before the plume takes the view, and fights it level. It comes down hard, upright.
do morale A 3

card e_entry_wait
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when flag arrive_wait
when is A abort_who
text Aerocapture. Three minutes of plasma blackout, eight ships silent in turn. Seven come out the far side on time. {A}'s comes out nine seconds late: nine seconds of nothing on the net, the call for a manual corridor correction ready on {A}'s tongue. Then {A}'s voice, reading out the orbit numbers, flat and in order.
do morale A 3

card e_entry_clear
type event
cat arrival
due
once
days 42 42
roles A
when !flag arrive_hold
when !flag arrive_wait
when is A abort_who
text Entry interface in clear air. Three minutes of plasma blackout, eight ships silent in turn. At the landing burn one of {A}'s engines lights late, a long half second, and the engine-out call is half out of {A}'s mouth when it catches. The ground comes up exactly where the maps said.
do morale A 3

card w_zodiac
type event
cat wonder
days 8 20
weight 10
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text Cabin dark, Sun behind the hull, {A} sees the zodiacal light with no air in the way: a long faint cone of comet dust, lit from behind. From home it is a smudge at dusk. Out here it is a road. {A} turns the screen brightness down to keep it.
do morale A 3

card w_milky
type event
cat wonder
days 23 23
due
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text {A} kills every light and waits twenty minutes for night eyes. The Milky Way comes up with the dark lanes in it, the ones no backyard ever shows. {A} names the ones in the book, then starts on the rest.
do trait A curious 2

card w_moon_pair
type event
cat wonder
days 22 22
due
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text Through the long lens Earth and the Moon share one frame now, close as two buttons on a coat. {A} sends a week of them home: "You are here. Both of you."
do morale A 3

# Round 24: the ledger. The bureaucracy's grimmest form, read aloud as written.
card g_ledger
type beat
cat grim
days 12 30
weight 6
once
roles A
when cond A ok
text The ground's weekly losses ledger comes up for {A}'s signature: two seed trays, one filter, eleven percent of spares, all within tolerance. Procedure says read it aloud before signing. {A} reads it to the cabin fan and signs. Tolerance has a column for crew. It is not blank.
